    "description": "A wrapper is a custom way to access remote resources. It is designed to look like accessing a file, on the file system, but using other drivers than the ones of the hard drive. It is based on a configuration string, which looks like a URL: ``ftp://www.site.com/file.txt``, where the part before the ``://`` is the protocol.\n\nAmong the predefined PHP wrappers, there are ``http://``, ``ftp://``, ``zlib://``, ``phar://``, ``rar://``, ``expect://``.",
